---
module: concepts
func_id: validate-concepts
---

***conformance tests***

# valid-tree
A tree with the definition `- ⟨Task⟩ is a thing to do.` and the functionality markdown `A ⟨Task⟩ is added by ⟨Implementation⟩.` has no error.

# undefined-concept
A tree with the definition `- ⟨Task⟩ is a thing to do.` and the functionality markdown `A ⟨User⟩ adds a ⟨Task⟩.` gives exactly the error `Syntax error: Concept ⟨User⟩ is not defined in the definitions. functional specs: A ⟨User⟩ adds a ⟨Task⟩.`.

# defined-twice
A tree with the definitions `- ⟨Task⟩ is x.` and `- ⟨Task⟩ is y.` gives an error starting with `Syntax error: Concepts were defined multiple times: ⟨Task⟩`.

# predefined-redefined
A tree with the definition `- ⟨Implementation⟩ is mine.` gives an error starting with `Syntax error: Concepts were defined multiple times: ⟨Implementation⟩`.

# words-between-colons-are-not-concepts
A tree whose implementation req is `- Time is 12:30 and ratio 1 : 2.` and that has no definitions has no error.

***acceptance tests***
